        "source-04-foveated-rendering-a-state-of-the-art-survey--2a4e30f52f30",
        "source-05-interactive-level-of-detail-rendering-of-large-graphs--df4eb719b5f7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "body": "The sources broadly agree that graphics systems gain scale by accepting controlled approximations. Crowd impostors, foveated rendering, skeleton-based edge bundling, and large-graph level-of-detail methods all replace uniform geometric or visual fidelity with context-sensitive representations. The disagreement is not a direct contradiction in the evidence but a difference in what each method is willing to lose: foveated rendering aims to preserve perceived quality while lowering peripheral detail, edge bundling explicitly accepts overdraw and direction distortion for coarse connectivity exploration, and crowd rendering manages popping, texture memory, and variety through impostor corrections and compressed storage. Shadercoding adds a complementary stance by treating constraints as part of the aesthetic and performative value, not only as engineering compromises.",
      "citation_anchor_ids": [
        "anchor-shadercoding",
        "anchor-crowd-rendering",
        "anchor-edge-bundling",
        "anchor-foveated-rendering"
      ],
