        "source-04-foveated-rendering-a-state-of-the-art-survey--2a4e30f52f30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "body": "The evidence base combines survey synthesis, algorithmic construction, performance measurement, and practice-based exposition. The foveated-rendering source classifies 90 reports from 1990 to 2021 into a three-dimensional taxonomy of input data, foveation principle, and rendering paradigm. The crowd-rendering source reports a concrete benchmark: 10,000 different humans in a 41,260-polygon village at 12 to 20 frames per second, supported by texture packing, compression, recoloring, and impostor-plane correction. The graph sources give algorithmic pipelines and measured scalability, including image-space distance transforms for skeleton bundling and linear-cost or sub-second overview rendering for large graph datasets. The shadercoding source supplies the conceptual and technical vocabulary connecting GPU programs, mathematical fluency, raymarching, and live performance.",
